        "module": "Approvals",
        "description": "omitting app-version silently returns a reduced payload",
        "detail": "The platform selects a response serializer from the app-version header. With no such header it answers 200 but strips every step and approver uuid, so a document cannot be approved and the cause is invisible — the call looks successful. Same effect on the approval-flows list, which switches between numeric ids and encoded uuids. The suite now always sends app-version.",
        "note": "worked around in the suite by always sending app-version — decide whether the default should be the full payload",
        "highlight": false,
        "client": "both",
        "endpoint": "GET /api/fx_responses/{uuid}/get_approvals",
        "evidence": "measured: no header -> approver.uuid undefined; 9.4.349 -> uuid present"
